    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Related\n\n- https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2542#issuecomment-5504481864\n\n### Problem\n\nSee \"Steps to reproduce\".\n\nDefinitely no one in their right mind would use the statuscolumn like this, but a crash is still worth fixing. The issue was discovered while using [mini.statuscolumn](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2542) with around 10 columns.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nvim.o.signcolumn = \"yes\"\nvim.o.statuscolumn = string.rep(\"%s\", 100)\n```\n\n```lua\nvim.o.number = true\nvim.o.statuscolumn = string.rep(\"%l\", 100)\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo crash.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1489+g f1d89e874a\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Btw\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.17.0 (94e7c887)\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
